# The places worth the walk (docs/VISION.md §3, §8), visited through real keys:
# read from a distance, named on arrival, opened with E, and on the map after.
#
#   tools/tour.sh tours/landmarks.tour --seed=1 --hour=10 --weather=clear:0
#
# THE FAR FRAMES ARE SHOT AT THE PLAY CAMERA. The first version of this tour
# zoomed to 26-30 for every silhouette — twice what a player is ever given — so
# every frame that said "from its own land" was a picture of a camera nobody has.
# A landmark's reach is now the camera's (`Landmarks.read_reach`), and the way to
# stand at it is to walk away from the place up the screen — about seven tiles,
# which is what `walk 0,-1 ... run` is doing in each of the far shots below — and
# the frame fails if the silhouette is not still in it. Further than that and a
# landmark is not dim, it is off the picture.
#
# One per landscape, four landscapes, each shot three times: the silhouette in
# its own land, the place close to, and what it gave. The order of the three is
# the order a landmark is meant to be experienced in, and it is the whole of what
# this package is for — a landscape you can see something in from across it, and
# something in it when you get there.

coast calm

# THE DROWNED LIGHT, on the coast. Backed off UP the screen — which is away from
# the camera, so the tower ends up on the near side of the frame where its head
# carries above the bottom edge (Landmarks.read_reach) — at the zoom the game is
# really played at. Ten tiles is as far as this camera lets a tower be read from,
# and that is the honest picture of it: a shape before it is a name.
place lighthouse
wait 0.6
walk 0,-1 1.4 run
wait 0.5
await landmark:lighthouse 12
shot 01-the-drowned-light-across-its-own-headland with landmark:lighthouse,land:coast

# And the tower is a THING, not a picture of one. Back at its face, walk INTO it:
# the stonework stops the body, which nothing in this package did at all until
# the masses were written. Pushed each way round the compass from its own face,
# because which way the tower lies from its cache is the island's business and
# not the tour's: one of the four drives into the stonework and is stopped by it,
# and `await landmark_wall` fails the tour if none of them is.
place lighthouse
wait 0.4
walk -1,1 0.7
walk 1,1 0.7
walk 1,-1 0.7
walk -1,-1 0.7
await landmark_wall 4
shot 02-the-stonework-stops-the-body with landmark:lighthouse

# Close to: the lamp room open to the weather, and the locker somebody dragged
# out of it standing in front. Round to its own face, which is where the hands go.
place lighthouse
zoom 10
wait 0.6
await landmark_cache 8
shot 03-the-drowned-light with landmark:lighthouse,landmark_cache

# And what was in it. One roll, once and for good (tests/landmarks/test_loot.gd).
press use 0.3
await took 8
# The slate wakes on anything taken, and a frame shot the instant it does is a
# picture of a pane half way up. Let it settle: what the place gave is meant to
# be read off the glass.
wait 1.6
shot 04-what-the-light-held with landmark:lighthouse
zoom 15

# THE FIRE TOWER: its stair gone, and the last person's kit still on the deck
# above where it was. It stands on a rise in three landscapes, and which one this
# seed's first tower is standing on is the world's business, not the tour's.
place firewatch
wait 0.6
walk 0,-1 1.4 run
wait 0.5
await landmark:firewatch 12
shot 05-the-fire-tower-from-across-its-rise with landmark:firewatch
place firewatch
zoom 10
wait 0.5
await landmark_cache 8
press use 0.3
await took 8
wait 1.6
shot 06-what-the-tower-held with landmark:firewatch
zoom 15

# THE CAST STONES: what stood here before the machines, with the fallen ones
# recast in concrete round rebar and set back up, and a survey plate bolted to
# the tallest of them.
place cast_stones
wait 0.6
walk 0,-1 1.4 run
wait 0.5
await landmark:cast_stones 12
shot 07-the-cast-stones-in-their-own-land with landmark:cast_stones
place cast_stones
zoom 10
wait 0.5
await landmark_cache 8
press use 0.3
await took 8
wait 1.6
shot 08-what-the-ring-held with landmark:cast_stones
zoom 15

# THE GROWN HULK: a machine that died standing, and has been in one place long
# enough for the land to come up through it.
place grown_hulk
wait 0.6
walk 0,-1 1.4 run
wait 0.5
await landmark:grown_hulk 12
shot 09-the-grown-hulk-across-its-clearing with landmark:grown_hulk
place grown_hulk
zoom 10
wait 0.5
await landmark_cache 8
press use 0.3
await took 8
wait 1.6
shot 10-what-the-hulk-held with landmark:grown_hulk

# And every one of them is on the slate's survey now, and stays there: a place
# found is found for the rest of the game, whether or not it was ever opened
# (tests/landmarks/test_loot.gd holds that through a save). The frame is named
# for what it can actually be seen to hold — a mark over each place found, each
# drawn with its own shape (`LandmarkDef.mark`, `UiMapScreen.MARKS`) instead of
# the same diamond nine times — and not for a survey the picture does not show:
# the first version of this frame was called "four places on the survey" over
# 0.8% of the island explored and at most one legible glyph.
zoom 15
press map 0.2
await app:map 6
wait 0.4
shot 11-the-places-found-marked-on-the-survey with app:map,found:lighthouse#1,found:grown_hulk#1
press map 0.2
